  "rounds": {
    "1": {
      "note": "In Cantonese a <b>classifier</b> (measure word) sits between a number — or 呢 (ni1, this) / 嗰 (go2, that) — and the noun, a bit like “a slice of” or “a pair of”. So “one book” is 一本書 (jat1 bun2 syu1), literally “one [classifier] book”. Different nouns take different classifiers, but 個 (go3) is the safe all-purpose one when you’re unsure.",
      "words": [
        {
          "id": "classifiers-001",
          "c": "個",
          "j": "go3",
          "e": "General classifier"
        },
        {
          "id": "classifiers-002",
          "c": "隻",
          "j": "zek3",
          "e": "Classifier: animals / one of a pair"
        },
        {
          "id": "classifiers-003",
          "c": "條",
          "j": "tiu4",
          "e": "Classifier: long things"
        },
        {
